Uploading beats on Beat22 helps you reach thousands of artists. Here are quick answers to common questions about the upload process. Whether you're a new seller or just need a quick refresher, this guide will help you upload confidently and correctly.

1.  ### **How do I upload a beat on Beat22 Studio?**
    

Uploading a beat is simple. Just log in to your seller account and **click on the button at the top right of the page**

![Uploading a beat is simple. Just log in to your seller account and click on the button at the top right of](/images/2025/06/upload.png)

. You’ll be guided through a step-by-step process covering:

-   Metadata entry (Beat title, type, genre, instruments, mood, tempo, tags, etc.)
-   Media upload (Tagged MP3, Cover Art, Untagged WAV, and Stems in ZIP format)
-   License and pricing
-   Optional settings like enabling negotiations for exclusive beats

For a detailed walkthrough, read our full article: [/how-to-upload-beats/](/2025/06/19/how-to-upload-beats/)

2.  ### **What audio file formats are supported?**
    

Beat22 supports the following file types:

-   Tagged MP3
-   WAV
-   WAV + STEMS (.ZIP Format)

3.  ### **Should I upload stems with or without effects?**
    

This depends on your production style and the needs of potential buyers.

-   Generally recommended: Upload stems without effects, so artists and engineers have full flexibility while mixing.
-   Exception: If an effect is crucial to the beat's vibe, you may choose to leave it on.

Use your best judgment based on what an artist or their engineer would expect from a professional stem pack.

4.  ### **What are Beat Tags and why do they matter?**
    

Beat tags are keywords (similar to hashtags) that help categorize your beat and make it more discoverable on the marketplace. Tags can describe:

-   Genre (e.g., #Trap, #Drill, #LoFi)
-   Mood (e.g., #Dark, #Uplifting)
-   Instrument (e.g., #Piano, #808)
-   Style or influence (e.g., #DrakeTypeBeat, #IndianDrill)

Beat22’s search algorithm uses these tags to match beats with artist preferences. The right tags can significantly boost your visibility and sales. So, tag wisely!

### **Final Tip: Upload with Intent**

Uploading isn’t just about getting your beat online. It’s about presenting it professionally from accurate metadata to clean stems and strategic tags. This gives buyers a great first impression and increases your chances of making a sale.

If you’re serious about growing your brand as a music producer, take the time to upload properly.
